% =============================================================================
% fpga_measured.tex — WITH-LOGS variant of Table~\ref{tab:fpga}.
%
% HOW TO USE
%   1. Obtain the four board logs from the collaborator's machine.
%   2. Copy this file to  data/fpga_measured.tex  (drop the .template suffix).
%   3. Replace each XXX with the measured cycle count.
%   4. Build with:  make fpga     -> produces main-with-fpga.pdf
%
% The default `make` target does NOT include this file and produces a paper
% that makes no FPGA measurement claim, so a submittable PDF always exists.
%
% WHAT TO EXTRACT FROM EACH LOG
%   xsim cycles : the "[PERF] GPU g: perf_total=..." lines. Take the MAX over
%                 all g, NOT GPU 0's value. (Recording GPU 0 alone was the
%                 defect found on 2026-07-27; it understated cycles on 54% of
%                 runs because an idle GPU 0 is common when the reduction root
%                 lands elsewhere.)
%   FPGA cycles : vio_perf_cycles from the Hardware Manager VIO probe, or the
%                 seven-segment readout, per top_fpga_interactive.sv.
%
% Delta is computed as 100*(fpga-xsim)/xsim. If the two disagree, say so and
% explain it -- a non-zero delta is a finding about the toolchain, not a
% failure. Do not round a real disagreement to 0.00.
% =============================================================================
